  "question": {
    "text": "The magnetic field due to a current in a straight wire segment of length $L$ at a point on\r\nits perpendicular bisector at a distano $r(r>>L)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "UDyaj",
      "text": "decreases as $\\frac{1}{r}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bN4Bz",
      "text": "decreases as $\\frac{1}{r^{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RDr1h",
      "text": "decreases as $\\frac{1}{r^{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0NOad",
      "text": "approaches a finite limit as $r \\rightarrow \\infty$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "By Biot-Savart's law, the magnetic field due to a current carrying wire is\r\n$$\r\nB=\\frac{\\mu_{0}}{4 \\pi} \\cdot \\frac{I d l \\sin \\theta}{r^{2}}\r\n$$\r\nSo,\r\n$$\r\nB=\\frac{1}{r^{2}}\r\n$$\r\nSo, the magnetic field due to current decreases as inverse square of distance of the point of observation.",
    "image": null
  },
